# house-pause-save-nav — open the PAUSE Save submenu (ESC → 3×down → Z), then
# DRIVE THE PICKER NAV: scroll DOWN through the slot list (the c894 row slide +
# the occupied slot-0 card scrolling up under the NO-DATA cards), scroll back
# UP, then B to close.  Verifies M4b (FUN_0047f5bc — pause_save_submenu_update).
# Derived from house-pause-save (load fa7c82 → HOUSE free-roam idle,
# {phasepin 80}+{rngseed [80,19937]}); the open path is identical.
#
# Initial picker state on open: slot 0 is the only occupied save, so
# last_slot==0 ⇒ cursor=0, scroll=0.  From there:
#   DOWN ×5: cursor 0→1→2 (in-window, no slide) →3→4→5 (each crosses the
#            window bottom ⇒ a c894 slide, scroll 0→1→2→3).
#   UP  ×4: cursor 5→4→3 (in-window) →2→1 (crosses the window top ⇒ c894
#            slide, scroll 3→2→1).
#   B: close the submenu (sub_dir→0, slides back to the option list).
# Presses are 3 frames, spaced ~14 so each c894 slide (4 frames) settles before
# the next press (a press mid-slide is swallowed, matching the engine).
#
# Sync — TWO rebases.  (1) the option-list nav + Z that OPEN the submenu rebase
# on PAUSE_READY (the pause-load-done edge gated on scene 9, the M4 sync point).
# (2) the PICKER NAV rebases on SAVE_PICKER_READY (sub_anim==10 with Save
# selected — the submenu becomes navigable).  This second rebase is essential:
# the async pause-asset load makes PAUSE_READY fire at a per-side-VARIABLE point
# in the open ramp (port ~1f, retail ~1800f), so PAUSE_READY+offset inputs reach
# the picker at a DIFFERENT picker-time per side, beating the selected card's
# breathe (sin(g_save_picker_frame·0.1)).  Anchoring the nav on SAVE_PICKER_READY
# makes the inputs picker-time-relative ⇒ cursor/scroll AND breathe align 1:1.
# embedded save: fa7c820333914d2a045f1003dc78c4b65fb04235e8d37f032c0f1e0aeb761c54
